# Where everything lives

Project knowledge is split across focused rule files, each loaded only when relevant. This map is always loaded so the agent always knows where to look next.

## Always loaded

- `core.mdc` — mission, stack, design principles, what-not-to-do
- `execution.mdc` — agent behavior discipline (search-first, partner mindset, anti-hallucination, two-strikes rule, verification)
- `plan-map.mdc` — this file

## Auto-loaded when touching code (glob-scoped)

- `conventions.mdc` — language, lint, styling, pnpm scripts (`src/**`, `worker/**`, `*.config.*`, `package.json`)
- `architecture.mdc` — layers, import rules (`src/**`, `worker/**`)

## Auto-loaded by topic (description-scoped)

- `product.mdc` — game rules, UX, multiplayer, PWA
- `roadmap.mdc` — waves, acceptance tests, deferred items
- `decisions.mdc` — resolved decisions ledger
- `api-design.mdc` — Workers, rooms, WebSocket protocol (when editing `worker/`)

## Operational (read on demand only)

- `.implementation/wave-N/phase-X.Y.md` — single-phase log. Load **only** when a prompt references a phase (e.g. `/implement phase-1.1`).

## Documentation files

- `README.md` — human setup, deploy, env vars. Not loaded by Cursor.
- `AGENTS.md` — pointer for non-Cursor agents. Not loaded by Cursor.

## Repo layout (target)

```
src/
  game/           # pure rules engine (no React)
  features/       # lobby, board, setup, online client
  shared/         # ui primitives, styles, hooks, utils
worker/           # Cloudflare Worker + Durable Object(s)
public/           # PWA icons, static assets
.implementation/  # phase plans
```

## Not yet needed

- `data-model.mdc` — add if persistent DB beyond Durable Object memory
